{"translation":{"id":"fra_jnd","name":"Bible J.N. Darby","website":"https://ebible.org/Scriptures/details.php?id=frajnd","licenseUrl":"https://ebible.org/Scriptures/details.php?id=frajnd","licenseNotes":null,"shortName":"JND","englishName":"French: Bible J.N. Darby","language":"fra","textDirection":"ltr","sha256":"121a3f4841e42965f22ebebcf5a8578a12578ec30eaf1ca7ae4e46d5d85ccb80","availableFormats":["json"],"listOfBooksApiLink":"/api/fra_jnd/books.json","numberOfBooks":66,"totalNumberOfChapters":1189,"totalNumberOfVerses":31170,"languageName":"français","languageEnglishName":"French"},"book":{"id":"PSA","translationId":"fra_jnd","name":"Les Psaumes","commonName":"Les Psaumes","title":"Les Psaumes","order":19,"numberOfChapters":150,"sha256":"4c48a766d24644f7ef347ae1395ef8ddb5d363cc30acf1733162d22f071b120e","firstChapterNumber":1,"firstChapterApiLink":"/api/fra_jnd/PSA/1.json","lastChapterNumber":150,"lastChapterApiLink":"/api/fra_jnd/PSA/150.json","totalNumberOfVerses":2527},"chapter":{"number":12,"content":[{"type":"verse","number":1,"content":[{"text":"Au chef de musique. Sur Sheminith. Psaume de David.","poem":1}]},{"type":"verse","number":2,"content":[{"text":"Sauve, Éternel ! car l’homme pieux n’est plus, car les fidèles ont disparu d’entre les fils des hommes.","poem":1}]},{"type":"verse","number":3,"content":[{"lineBreak":true},{"text":"Ils parlent la fausseté","poem":1},{"noteId":31},{"text":"l’un à l’autre ; [leur] lèvre est flatteuse, ils parlent d’un cœur double","poem":1},{"noteId":32},{"text":".","poem":1}]},{"type":"verse","number":4,"content":[{"lineBreak":true},{"text":"L’Éternel retranchera toutes les lèvres flatteuses, la langue qui parle de grandes choses,","poem":1}]},{"type":"verse","number":5,"content":[{"lineBreak":true},{"text":"Ceux qui disent : Par nos langues nous prévaudrons, nos lèvres sont à nous ; qui est seigneur sur nous ?","poem":1}]},{"type":"verse","number":6,"content":[{"lineBreak":true},{"text":"À cause de l’oppression des affligés, à cause du gémissement des pauvres, maintenant je me lèverai, dit l’Éternel ; je mettrai en sûreté [celui] contre qui on souffle.","poem":1}]},{"type":"verse","number":7,"content":[{"lineBreak":true},{"text":"Les paroles de l’Éternel sont des paroles pures, un argent affiné dans le creuset de terre","poem":1},{"noteId":33},{"text":", coulé sept fois.","poem":1}]},{"type":"verse","number":8,"content":[{"lineBreak":true},{"text":"Toi, Éternel ! tu les garderas, tu les préserveras de cette génération, à toujours.","poem":1}]},{"type":"verse","number":9,"content":[{"lineBreak":true},{"text":"Les méchants se promènent de toutes parts quand la bassesse est élevée parmi les fils des hommes.","poem":1}]}],"footnotes":[{"noteId":31,"caller":"a","text":"ou : la vanité.","reference":{"chapter":12,"verse":3}},{"noteId":32,"caller":"b","text":"litt. : un cœur et un cœur.","reference":{"chapter":12,"verse":3}},{"noteId":33,"caller":"c","text":"ou : en terre.","reference":{"chapter":12,"verse":7}}]},"thisChapterLink":"/api/fra_jnd/PSA/12.json","thisChapterAudioLinks":{},"nextChapterApiLink":"/api/fra_jnd/PSA/13.json","nextChapterAudioLinks":{},"previousChapterApiLink":"/api/fra_jnd/PSA/11.json","previousChapterAudioLinks":{},"numberOfVerses":9}